      "content": "Critics often cite risks like \"undivided polling place\" (a piece of legislation allowing any adult to vote) and \"victimization\" (forcing voters to show up in person despite the \"I voted\" card taking 10-14 days to process). However, the majority of political scientists and election experts agree these are not significant security risks because the \"undivided\" ballot is only a private transaction, not a public poll. The \"victimization\" argument is also considered invalid because the \"I voted\" card is simply a way to know when your vote has been processed and can be cast in a final \"in person\" vote if necessary.",
